#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
coupang - agent-native CLI for Coupang Taiwan (www.tw.coupang.com, TWD). No checkout.

Zero dependencies (Python 3.8+ stdlib). Every command supports --json and
returns the {ok, data|error} envelope used by the other ~/Projects CLIs.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 api, 2 usage, 3 auth, 4 net/blocked.

Endpoints, measured 2026-10-29 with real requests
--------------------------------------------------
Search (Next.js RSC HTML, preprocessedProducts in self.__next_f.push):
  GET https://www.tw.coupang.com/np/search?q=<q>&sorter=<sort>&minPrice=<min>&maxPrice=<max>&page=<p>
      Contains preprocessedProducts array with productId, itemId, vendorItemId,
      title, price, originPrice, discountRate, ratingAverage, ratingCount,
      isRocket, outOfStock, deliveryInfo, linkURL.
      sorter: scoreDesc (relevance/default), salePriceAsc (price low->high),
              salePriceDesc (price high->low), saleCountDesc (sales count),
              latestAsc (newest).
      Plain HTTPS works when valid session cookies + Edge UA are sent;
      when challenged by Akamai Bot Manager, auto-falls back to CDP background tab.
      CAVEAT (measured 2026-10-30, confirmed on the live site's own sort control
      and product pages in a background tab):
        - Sponsored/ad slots (product link carries sourceType=srp_product_ads)
          are pinned into the result list identically regardless of sort or
          page - left in, they cause page N+1 to repeat page N's items and
          break monotonic price order. The CLI drops every sponsored item.
        - A small number of regular (non-ad) listings genuinely display the
          literal price "$99,999" on their own product page - a seller-side
          placeholder for a not-really-purchasable item. The CLI drops any
          item priced exactly NT$99,999.
        - Coupang's own salePriceAsc/salePriceDesc ordering is reliable for
          roughly the first 7-8 items per request but drifts out of order
          beyond that (confirmed on the live salePriceDesc page: positions
          8-13 were NOT monotonic). So the CLI collects candidates across
          as many remote search pages as needed (up to 6), dedupes by base
          product id (the same product can list several price variants
          under different itemId/vendorItemId - only the first-seen variant
          is kept so a product never appears twice across pages), sorts
          client-side for --sort price/price-desc, and paginates --page/
          --limit from that clean pool. Very low prices (NT$1-$14) were
          verified real on the product's own page (legitimate single-unit/
          clearance variants), not misparsed per-unit prices - left in.

Product page (HTML + JSON-LD + Option Table):
  GET https://www.tw.coupang.com/products/<id>?itemId=<itemId>&vendorItemId=<vendorItemId>
      (also /vp/products/<id> which 302-redirects to /products/<id>)
      LD+JSON script[type="application/ld+json"] holds @type: Product with name,
      brand, sku, priceSpecification (strikethrough / original), price (offer),
      availability, aggregateRating, image list.
      Options table div.option-table-list__option holds variants / selectable specs
      (e.g. 2袋, 28袋, etc.) with prices and selection state.

Account / Member Whoami:
  GET https://cart.tw.coupang.com/api/node/cart/content?isLogin=true
      Returns {rCode: "RET0000", rData: {common: {isLogin: true/false},
      shoppingCart: {memberSrl, totalItemCount, ...}}}.
  GET https://www.tw.coupang.com/
      Logged-in HTML contains "Una*********立即前往我的酷澎" and "親愛的 Una*********".

Cart (cart.tw.coupang.com & www.tw.coupang.com):
  GET  https://cart.tw.coupang.com/api/node/cart/content?isLogin=true
       Full cart content: shoppingCart.totalItemCount, totalSalePrice,
       totalDiscountPrice, totalDeliveryPrice, totalOrderPrice,
       skuBundleSet.allBundleList[].shoppingCartItemList[] with cartItemId,
       productId, vendorItemId, productName, vendorItemName, quantity, salePrice.
  POST https://www.tw.coupang.com/next-api/order/add-cart
       Body: {"items[]":["<vendorItemId>: <qty>"],"clickProductId":productId,
              "landProductId":str(productId),"clickItemId":itemId,
              "cartItemId":itemId,"productId":productId}
       Header: Content-Type: application/json
       Executed in background tab to pass Akamai bot verification.
  POST https://cart.tw.coupang.com/api/node/cart/quantity?cartItemId=<id>&quantity=<N>&isAllChecked=true&isLogin=true
       Body: {}
  POST https://cart.tw.coupang.com/api/node/cart/deleteItems?cartItemIds[]=<id>&itemStatus=CHECKED&isLogin=true
       Body: {}

Login:
  Never passwords/OTP. `coupang login` takes a DevTools `Cookie:` request header: from
  stdin when piped, else from the clipboard (exit 2 + instructions if the clipboard
  holds no Coupang Cookie header). Also --from-clipboard / --cookie-stdin.
  `coupang login --from-browser` (opt-in) reads cookies from Edge on COUPANG_CDP
  (default http://127.0.0.1:9222). If not signed in, opens
  https://member.tw.coupang.com/login/login.pang in a background tab and waits
  (--wait 300) while you sign in there. Session is saved to ~/.config/coupang/state.json
  (mode 0600) or keyring (--keyring). COUPANG_COOKIE overrides both.

No checkout / payment / order placement:
  By design, no checkout, order placement or payment endpoint is ever called.

Unofficial. Undocumented, private API - it can break without warning.
